        <fig id="article-25981.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Normal Pressure Hydrocephalus Imaging. Computed tomography (CT) contributes to the visualization of anatomic brain changes but lacks sufficient specificity for diagnosis when used in isolation. Contributed by S Lange, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Normal__pressure__hydrocephalus" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
