      <floats-group id="article-25981.s21">
        <fig id="article-25981.image.f4" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Imaging Hallmarks of Idiopathic Normal Pressure Hydrocephalus. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) plays a central role in the evaluation of suspected iNPH by documenting ventriculomegaly and characteristic morphologic features that support diagnosis within the appropriate clinical context. Contributed by K Margetis, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="DESH" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
